{"name":"Northern Exposure","hex":"#bfc7d4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"northern","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, facing, situated in, or related to the north; northerly.","Blowing from the north; northerly."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An inhabitant of the northern regions; a northerner.","The northern pike."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/northern"},{"term":"exposure","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The condition of being exposed, uncovered, or unprotected.","Lack of protection from weather or the elements."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exposure"}],"entries":[{"title":"Northern Exposure (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Northern Exposure is the second mix album by British DJ duo Sasha & John Digweed. Released on 27 September 1996, it is the first in their Northern Exposure series, followed by Northern Exposure 2 in 1997 and Northern Exposure: Expeditions in 1999. There is both a British edition released by Ministry of Sound and an American edition released by Ultra Records in 1997. The British package contains both CDs, whereas the American only has the first disc. In 2013, the album was certified silver in the UK."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/0e/Ne1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Northern_Exposure_(album)","wikidata":"Q7058337"},{"title":"BBC Northern Ireland","blocks":[{"text":"BBC Northern Ireland is a division of the BBC and the main public broadcaster in Northern Ireland. It is widely available across both Northern Ireland and the Republic of Ireland."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/BBC_Northern_Ireland_2022.svg/330px-BBC_Northern_Ireland_2022.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BBC_Northern_Ireland","wikidata":"Q2876741"},{"title":"Northern Exposure","blocks":[{"text":"Northern Exposure is an American comedy-drama television series that originally aired on CBS from July 12, 1990, to July 26, 1995, with a total of 110 episodes. The series follows the eccentric residents in the fictitious town of Cicely, Alaska. Rob Morrow starred as New York City native Dr. Joel Fleischman, whose med school tuition was underwritten by the government of Alaska in exchange for him practicing medicine for four years in the state."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c9/Northern_Exposure-Intertitle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Northern_Exposure","wikidata":"Q301345"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/BBC_Northern_Ireland_Belfast.jpg/500px-BBC_Northern_Ireland_Belfast.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/BBC_Northern_Ireland_Belfast.jpg/1280px-BBC_Northern_Ireland_Belfast.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/BBC_Northern_Ireland_Belfast.jpg/500px-BBC_Northern_Ireland_Belfast.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Broadcasting House, Belfast, Headquarters of the BBC in Northern Ireland.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABBC_Northern_Ireland_Belfast.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Blackstaff_House%2C_Belfast.jpg/500px-Blackstaff_House%2C_Belfast.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Blackstaff_House%2C_Belfast.jpg/500px-Blackstaff_House%2C_Belfast.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"BBC Blackstaff House","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlackstaff_House%2C_Belfast.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Cynthia_Geary_Rob_Morrow_and_Janine_Turner_at_the_45th_Emmy_Awards.jpg/500px-Cynthia_Geary_Rob_Morrow_and_Janine_Turner_at_the_45th_Emmy_Awards.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Cynthia_Geary_Rob_Morrow_and_Janine_Turner_at_the_45th_Emmy_Awards.jpg/500px-Cynthia_Geary_Rob_Morrow_and_Janine_Turner_at_the_45th_Emmy_Awards.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Left to right: Cynthia Geary, Rob Morrow, and Janine Turner at the 1993 Emmy Awards","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACynthia_Geary_Rob_Morrow_and_Janine_Turner_at_the_45th_Emmy_Awards.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Peg_Phillips_and_Barry_Cobin.jpg/500px-Peg_Phillips_and_Barry_Cobin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Peg_Phillips_and_Barry_Cobin.jpg/500px-Peg_Phillips_and_Barry_Cobin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Peg Phillips and Barry Corbin at the 1993 Emmy Awards","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APeg_Phillips_and_Barry_Cobin.jpg"}],"sounds":{"northern":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/61/En-us-northern.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/6/61/En-us-northern.ogg/En-us-northern.ogg.mp3"}],"exposure":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/85/En-us-exposure.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikim